From 0002-gmux-i915-switcheroo Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Krzysztof Kowalski <krzysztof7kowalski@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0002/0005] vga_switcheroo: add client reinit callback for GPU
 power-cycle recovery

On muxed laptops the muxer handler (e.g. apple-gmux on the MacBook Pro)
can cut power to the discrete GPU much deeper than a plain D3 suspend:
the gmux microcontroller tears down the core/VRAM/PCIe power rails, which
wipes the device's VBIOS/option ROM and PCIe link training state.

Today vga_switcheroo only calls the client's ->set_gpu_state()/runtime
resume after the handler reinstates power. On Kepler (nouveau) that is
not enough: the card frequently fails to come back from such a hard
power-cycle ("VBIOS znika", stuck in D3, PCIe link speed regression),
because nothing tells the driver that the firmware state was lost.

Add an optional ->reinit callback to struct vga_switcheroo_client_ops
and invoke it right after the handler's ->power_state(ON) completes:

* vga_switchon() (manual IGD/DIS/ON switches): between power_state(ON)
  and set_gpu_state(ON), so the driver can reload the VBIOS before its
  resume path runs;
* vga_switcheroo_runtime_resume() (driver power control / runtime PM):
  after pci_resume_bus() and before the driver's runtime_resume, via the
  new vga_switcheroo_notify_reinit() helper.

The callback is optional; drivers that do not implement it are
unaffected. This is the missing plumbing to let nouveau/i915 reinitialize
the GPU after an apple-gmux power-cycle (MacBookPro11,3 retina).

Signed-off-by: Krzysztof Kowalski <krzysztof7kowalski@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/vga/vga_switcheroo.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/vga_switcheroo.h   |  7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 36 insertions(+)

diff --git i/drivers/gpu/vga/vga_switcheroo.c w/drivers/gpu/vga/vga_switcheroo.c
index 22cf52b78..6f7e48304 100644
--- i/drivers/gpu/vga/vga_switcheroo.c
+++ w/drivers/gpu/vga/vga_switcheroo.c
@@ -667,12 +667,41 @@ static int vga_switcheroo_debugfs_open(struct inode *inode, struct file *file)
 	return single_open(file, vga_switcheroo_show, NULL);
 }

+/*
+ * vga_switcheroo_notify_reinit() - ask a client to reload firmware after a
+ * hard power-cycle.
+ *
+ * After the muxer handler has reinstated power to a GPU that was cut off, the
+ * device lost its VBIOS/option ROM and PCIe link training state. Give the
+ * bound client a chance to restore that state before its resume path runs.
+ * This mirrors the historical behaviour of the discrete GPU power management
+ * on muxed Apple laptops, where the gmux power-cycle is deeper than a plain
+ * D3 suspend and the driver must not rely on the runtime resume alone.
+ */
+static void vga_switcheroo_notify_reinit(struct pci_dev *pdev)
+{
+	struct vga_switcheroo_client *client;
+
+	mutex_lock(&vgasr_mutex);
+	client = find_client_from_pci(&vgasr_priv.clients, pdev);
+	if (client && client->ops->reinit)
+		client->ops->reinit(pdev);
+	mutex_unlock(&vgasr_mutex);
+}
+
 static int vga_switchon(struct vga_switcheroo_client *client)
 {
 	if (client->driver_power_control)
 		return 0;
 	if (vgasr_priv.handler->power_state)
 		vgasr_priv.handler->power_state(client->id, VGA_SWITCHEROO_ON);
+	/*
+	 * If the handler just reinstated power to a GPU that was previously
+	 * cut off (a hard power-cycle), the device lost its firmware state
+	 * (VBIOS, PCIe link). Let the client reload it before resuming.
+	 */
+	if (client->ops->reinit)
+		client->ops->reinit(client->pdev);
 	/* call the driver callback to turn on device */
 	client->ops->set_gpu_state(client->pdev, VGA_SWITCHEROO_ON);
 	client->pwr_state = VGA_SWITCHEROO_ON;
@@ -1038,6 +1067,12 @@ static int vga_switcheroo_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 	vga_switcheroo_power_switch(pdev, VGA_SWITCHEROO_ON);
 	mutex_unlock(&vgasr_mutex);
 	pci_resume_bus(pdev->bus);
+	/*
+	 * The handler's power_state(ON) above may have been a hard
+	 * power-cycle rather than a plain D3 wakeup. Give the driver a
+	 * chance to reload firmware (VBIOS) before its runtime_resume runs.
+	 */
+	vga_switcheroo_notify_reinit(pdev);
 	return dev->bus->pm->runtime_resume(dev);
 }

diff --git i/include/linux/vga_switcheroo.h w/include/linux/vga_switcheroo.h
index 7e6ac0114..97cd4e0af 100644
--- i/include/linux/vga_switcheroo.h
+++ w/include/linux/vga_switcheroo.h
@@ -134,6 +134,12 @@ struct vga_switcheroo_handler {
  * 	Mandatory. The client should return false if a user space process
  * 	has one of its device files open
  * @gpu_bound: notify the client id to audio client when the GPU is bound.
+ * @reinit: reload firmware (e.g. VBIOS) after a hard power-cycle.
+ * 	Optional. Called after the handler has reinstated power to a GPU
+ * 	that was previously cut off (powered down through the muxer, which
+ * 	is deeper than a plain D3 suspend). Such a power-cycle wipes the
+ * 	device's firmware state, so the driver must reload the VBIOS/option
+ * 	ROM and redo any device state it cannot get back from resume alone.
  *
  * Client callbacks. A client can be either a GPU or an audio device on a GPU.
  * The @set_gpu_state and @can_switch methods are mandatory, @reprobe may be
@@ -145,6 +151,7 @@ struct vga_switcheroo_client_ops {
 	void (*reprobe)(struct pci_dev *dev);
 	bool (*can_switch)(struct pci_dev *dev);
 	void (*gpu_bound)(struct pci_dev *dev, enum vga_switcheroo_client_id);
+	void (*reinit)(struct pci_dev *dev);
 };

 #if defined(CONFIG_VGA_SWITCHEROO)
--
2.46.0
